A constant can hold a fully known struct value.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    Defaults = |
        title String,
        year Int,
    |

    defaults #= Defaults("Moth", 2026)
]

Read its fields during compilation or use an ordinary field in runtime code:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    site_title #= defaults.title
    io.line(defaults.title)
]

The complete const record is not an ordinary runtime object. Use its fields
instead. A field that is itself a const record keeps the same restriction.

### Anonymous records

Anonymous construction uses
@../language-overview/#mon-syntax (MON syntax) and requires all fields to fold.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    settings #= (
        title = "Strategy",
        window = (width = 1280, height = 720),
    )

    width #= settings.window.width
]

Every field needs a name and a value. Anonymous construction creates a value,
not a named type. Use an explicit constructor for a named struct.
